READ-ONLY audit of /Users/konstantinbaltsat/whest-starterkit. Do NOT edit, write, commit, submit, or touch challenge targets/packages/submissions. Read source and report.

Deliver a precise technical audit:

A. e141 ESTIMATOR SOURCE
Locate the shipped e141 predictor (grep for e141, "predict", submission/package dirs, research/e141*). Give:
- the exact mathematical form of the estimator as implemented, function by function, with file:line refs;
- the sufficient statistics it computes at predict time;
- where randomness enters (Kerdock carrier construction, coordinate signs, pilot rows) and whether the randomness is seeded per-row/deterministic;
- exact loop structure and per-layer FLOP cost drivers (the audit says prefix matmuls layers 2-29 are 123.14e9 of 160e9 total — confirm from source what those matmuls' shapes are, i.e. what sketch width is used);
- what the "compact" representation is (bit-packed? b32/s2 vs b16/s3 refer to what?).

B. FLOPSCOPE ACCOUNTING (flopscope 0.9.1, whestbench 0.13.0)
- how FLOPs are counted per primitive; which primitives exist; anything that is free or undercounted;
- the wall-time → effective-compute conversion actually implemented (I infer effective = FLOPs + 1e11 × residual_seconds — confirm from source);
- memory tracking rules and the array-size limit;
- what counts as "predict time" vs setup/import time — specifically, is module-import-time or constant-table computation counted? Can precomputed constants be shipped as data instead of computed?
- whether loading a shipped weights/state file costs FLOPs.

C. LOCAL EVAL HARNESS
- how a candidate estimator is scored offline: which corpus, how truth is produced (analytic or Monte Carlo with replicas), split conventions (train 0:128 / validation 128:160 / reserved 160:192 appear in e159), seed conventions, how to generate FRESH synthetic networks + truth.
- the exact cost of generating a fresh truth replicate (time per network), since that bounds how big a synthetic training corpus could be.

D. EXPERIMENT DIRECTORY LEDGER
List every research/e*/ directory: name, RESULTS.md verdict line, and one-line reason. Include any that lack RESULTS.md (in-flight/abandoned).

E. SHIPPABLE STATE
- can the submission package include a binary weights/state file? evidence from packaging code or rules;
- observed package size and any size gate in the tooling.

Use rg/fd, read actual source. Cite file:line for every claim. Mark anything unverified as UNVERIFIED. Dense markdown output.
